From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm5: split reasoning on </think> even when thinking is "off"

GLM-5.3-Flash's chat template ends every prompt with an open <think>, also for
enable_thinking=false and reasoning_effort=none (which vLLM maps to
enable_thinking=false). The model therefore still reasons, but the glm45/glm47
parser (one adapter) trusted the flag and returned the whole output, thinking
included, as content. With VLLM_GLM53_FORCE_THINK_BOUNDARIES=1 the parser keeps
its reasoning state machine on, so </think> rather than the request flag
separates reasoning from content. It does not stop the model from thinking;
do not enable it for templates that close the think block themselves.
Default off.

diff --git a/vllm/parser/glm47_moe.py b/vllm/parser/glm47_moe.py
--- a/vllm/parser/glm47_moe.py
+++ b/vllm/parser/glm47_moe.py
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
 
 import functools
 import json
+import os
 from typing import TYPE_CHECKING
 
 import regex as re
@@ -189,6 +190,13 @@
             if thinking is None and enable_thinking is None
             else bool(thinking) or bool(enable_thinking)
         )
+        # Model-specific opt-in: GLM-5.3's shipped template always ends in
+        # an open <think>, even for enable_thinking=False / effort=none.
+        # Keep boundary parsing active so </think>, not a request flag,
+        # separates reasoning from content. This does NOT disable thinking.
+        # Do not enable for templates that end in an already closed think.
+        if os.environ.get("VLLM_GLM53_FORCE_THINK_BOUNDARIES", "0") == "1":
+            self.thinking_enabled = True
         kwargs.setdefault(
             "parser_engine_config",
             glm47_moe_config(thinking=self.thinking_enabled),
